{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvalidator\/issue"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/danglingPartID(_:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/durationBeforeDivisions(part:measure:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/unbalancedPartGroup(number:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/unknownInstrumentSound(_:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/unmatchedEndingStart(number:part:measure:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/unmatchedEndingStop(number:part:measure:)","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/unusedScorePart(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/message"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Issue"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/UsingIvorMXL"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An issue describes conformance the schema cannot express and the parser","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not enforce. The catalogue is deliberately confined to checks that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"sound on conforming input","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — a well-formed score never trips one —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so that a reported issue is always a genuine defect and never a false","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alarm. Every check runs against the normalized part-wise score, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"part","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"measure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" labels are the part ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and measure ","type":"text"},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"score.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opus is not checked at all: its schema is four elements and the parser","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already enforces nearly everything they constrain, so it passes straight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the validator.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two checks the schema-diff proposal listed as candidates are deliberately","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absent, because they cannot be decided soundly from the AST alone:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measure duration versus the prevailing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<time>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"text","text":" MusicXML permits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partial measures that are not flagged "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"implicit"},{"type":"text","text":" (pickups, measures split"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"across a repeat or a mid-measure meter change), so a short measure is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evidence of a defect."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Number-keyed spanner pairing (","type":"text"},{"code":"<slur>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"<tuplet>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"<wedge>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like).","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" level is reused across simultaneous voices, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spec expressly allows a spanner’s start and stop to appear in arbitrary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document order, so pairing them requires the per-voice onset timeline the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolver builds — not something the validator can settle. Unclosed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spanners are also a common, non-fatal real-world imperfection.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An issue found when validating an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDocument","type":"reference"},{"text":" against the MusicXML","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specification.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLValidatorV5IssueO","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Issue","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Issue","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLValidator.Issue","roleHeadin